        "original_id": "821863bc-4f84-5a1e-b2af-ebdd5961819c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georg Cantor, Vladimir Arnold\n- Concepts: transfinite number, transfinite\n- Topics: mathematicians, mathematical terminology\n\nFacts:\n- Georg Ferdinand Ludwig Philipp Cantor was born on March 3, 1845, and died on January 6, 1918.\n- Georg Cantor was a German mathematician.\n- Georg Cantor coined the term \"transfinite\" to avoid some implications of the word \"infinite\" for objects that were not finite.\n- Vladimir Igorevich Arnold was born on June 12, 1937, and died on June 3, 2010.\n- Vladimir Igorevich Arnold, also spelled Arnol'd, was a Soviet and Russian mathematician.",
